  "subRow": "Company, battalion two up",
  "note": "As IBB Annex U App 6 p 481 draws it: A and B Coys 1500 m wide with a 500 m gap and 500 m flanks (4500 m), forward centres 1000 m either side of the axis; C and D Coys in depth, one behind EACH forward Coy (C behind A, D behind B), side by side with the same 500 m gap. Depth 3000-4000 m from the forward edge back; laid at 3050 m, the short end, so D Coy (the reserve) reaches the forward Coys within the half hour of a Coy counter-attack (IBB S53 para 12b p 279; the choice of the short end a decision, E). Bn HQ (IBB S3 pp 22-24; p 23: placed centrally within the Bn locality, preferably behind the depth localities; a defended locality of 55 all ranks, concealed from the air, dug in, near the Bde axis with an alternative posn; laid about 500 m behind the depth Coys, between them (the distance a decision, E). The RRs, a section of two in each rifle Coy, sited first in the forward localities with an alternative each 200-300 m back (IBB S8 pp 38-42; IC p 367). Protective minefield (PlanObstacles, the user's trace of 28 Nov 2026): panels round the front of each forward Coy and its open flank, about 200 m out (IC s111 para 5 p 651), up to 250 m deep (IC s107 p 596), patrol lanes between them (IC s74 para 18 a p 394); the depth Coys' open flanks closed to contain a penetration (none beside the reserve: its way out kept clear) (IC s74 para 19 c p 395), their rear left open for the counter-attack. A screen 1 km ahead of the FDLs (AMP p 1.2) by a Pl of C Coy (IBB S54 para 4 c pp 284-285: its troops from the depth Coys).",
